      ⍝ suspended or pendant function ----------------------------------

      ⍝ regression (our own AP210-based cross-checking harness, 2026-09-25):
      ⍝ this whole suspend/)SI/→4-resume idiom, replayed through our
      ⍝ ALT ⎕EA HARNESS_INNER wrapper instead of a real interactive
      ⍝ session, was found to corrupt RUN_STMTS's own HARNESS_I loop
      ⍝ counter -- confirmed live: with these 4 statements included among
      ⍝ several thousand others, RUN_STMTS entered a genuine infinite
      ⍝ loop, jumping back ~2000 statements every time it reached the
      ⍝ second FUNC call and cycling forever instead of advancing. Not
      ⍝ diagnosed further (plausibly ⎕EA's error recovery interacting
      ⍝ badly with a *suspended*, not merely erroring, callee -- the same
      ⍝ general hazard class as the →4 statement itself, which our
      ⍝ extractor already excludes on its own). SKIPped rather than fixed
      ⍝ here, out of scope for this cross-checking task -- see
      ⍝ project_apl2_and_or_boolean_only.md.
      ]FILE_CTL SKIP_APL2
      ⎕FX 'FUNC' '1' '2' '!¯3' '4'
FUNC

      FUNC
1
2
DOMAIN ERROR
FUNC[3]  !¯3
         ^

      )SI
FUNC[3]
*

      →4
4

      ⎕FX 'FUNC' '21' '22' '23' '24'
FUNC

      FUNC
21
22
23
24

      ]FILE_CTL NO_SKIP

