      ⍝ Regression (Blake McBride, LanguageVariances.md #30, 2026-08-10):
      ⍝ execution properties must be inherited ("or-ed") from every
      ⍝ CALLING function too (apl2lrm.txt p.360-361), not just applied to
      ⍝ the function that carries them -- distinct from the "0 1 0 0 bar"
      ⍝ case above, where bar's OWN nonsuspendable property does NOT
      ⍝ propagate back up to its caller foo. Here it is the CALLER (CV /
      ⍝ FF2) that carries the property, and it must propagate DOWN to the
      ⍝ callee (GG) it invokes.
      ⍝
      )ERASE GG CV
      ⊣⎕FX 'GG' 'ZZZUNDEF'
      ⊣0 0 0 1 ⎕FX 'CV' 'GG'      ⍝ CV converts non-resource errors to DOMAIN
      CV
DOMAIN ERROR+
GG[1]  ZZZUNDEF
       ^

      ]FILE_CTL SKIP_APL2   ⍝ ⎕ET depends on the test harness
      ⎕ET
5 4

      →

      )ERASE GG FF2
      ⊣⎕FX 'GG' '!¯3'
      ⊣0 1 0 0 ⎕FX 'FF2' 'GG'     ⍝ FF2 is nonsuspendable
      ]FILE_CTL NO_SKIP
      FF2
DOMAIN ERROR
      GG
      ^^

      ⍝ nothing suspended: FF2's nonsuspendable property propagated to GG
      ⍝
      )SI
*

      )CHECK
OK      - no stale functions
OK      - no stale values
OK      - no stale indices
OK      - no duplicate parents

      ⍝ Bugs28 #16 regression: redefining a function that is bound as
      ⍝ the LO/RO operand of a *suspended* defined operator must be
      ⍝ refused, the same as for a function that is itself suspended/
      ⍝ executing -- otherwise the suspended frame is left holding a
      ⍝ dangling Function* (SEGFAULT at the next )CHECK).
      ⍝
      )CLEAR
CLEAR WS

      ⎕FX 'Z←FN16 B' 'Z←B'
FN16

      ⎕FX 'Z←A (LO OP2 RO) B' 'Z←A LO RO B'
OP2

      ⊥ OP2 FN16 0                  ⍝ VALUE ERROR; OP2[1] suspended with RO←FN16
VALUE ERROR+
OP2[1]  Z←A LO RO B
          ^

      ⍝ refused: ⎕FX returns an error line, not the function's name
      ⍝
      ⎕FX 'Z←FN16 B' 'Z←B+1'
1

      )CHECK
OK      - no stale functions
OK      - no stale values
OK      - no stale indices
OK      - no duplicate parents

      ⍝ once the suspended frame is gone, FN16 is unaffected
      ⍝
      )SIC
      FN16 5
5

      )CHECK
OK      - no stale functions
OK      - no stale values
OK      - no stale indices
OK      - no duplicate parents

      ⍝ regression (Blake McBride, Bugs28 #69, 2026-08-11): ⎕FX (and ∇)
      ⍝ used to accept a function whose name starts with λ (e.g. λ1) as
      ⍝ if it were an ordinary function -- is_lambda() goes by name alone,
      ⍝ so such a function reported itself as a genuine, machine-generated
      ⍝ lambda without ever having been through the actual lambda
      ⍝ bookkeeping (refcount etc.), corrupting later ⎕NC/⎕EX/)ERASE/)OFF
      ⍝ handling. λ is reserved for lambdas, same as λ←5 is already
      ⍝ refused for variables; now DEFN ERROR at fix/edit time instead.
      ⍝
      Z←⎕FX 'Z←λ1 B' 'Z←9'
      Z
1
      ⎕NC 'λ1'
¯1

∇Z←λ2 B
DEFN ERROR+
      ∇Z←λ2 B
            ^
 Z←9
∇
DEFN ERROR+
      ∇
      ^
      ⎕NC 'λ2'
¯1

      ⍝ regression (Blake McBride, Bugs28 #70, 2026-08-11): ⎕FX (and ∇)
      ⍝ used to accept a label that duplicates a header name (so the
      ⍝ label silently shadowed the argument/result) or another label (so
      ⍝ the last one silently won and the earlier one became unreachable)
      ⍝ -- ISO 13751 / APL2 require header names and labels to all be
      ⍝ distinct. Now refused at fix time (the ⎕FX result is the
      ⍝ offending row number, and the function is not defined at all).
      ⍝ Bugs35 #54: quietly, like any other bad line (no DEFN ERROR is
      ⍝ printed while ⎕FX returns the row anyway).
      ⍝
      Z1←⎕FX 'Z←F70a B' 'Z←B' 'B:'
      Z1
3
      ⎕NC 'F70a'
0

      Z2←⎕FX 'Z←F70b B' '→X' 'Z←0' 'X:Z←1' '→0' 'X:Z←2'
      Z2
6
      ⎕NC 'F70b'
0

      Z3←⎕FX 'Z←F70c B' 'Z←B' 'Z:'
      Z3
3
      ⎕NC 'F70c'
0

      ⍝ regression (Bugs28 #89): ⎕FX / ∇ accepted ⍺ ⍵ ⍶ ⍹ χ as a
      ⍝ function or argument name -- the tokenizer gives these their own
      ⍝ distinguished Symbol (not an ordinary SymbolTable entry), but
      ⍝ they still carry the generic TC_SYMBOL class every header
      ⍝ position's "is this a symbol" check accepted. The function
      ⍝ became callable under the reserved name, yet could not be
      ⍝ listed, expunged, or saved, and every redefinition leaked the
      ⍝ previous body. is_system_var() (UserFunction_header.cc) now
      ⍝ rejects them at every header position, the same way it already
      ⍝ rejected ⎕-names.
      ⍝
      ]FILE_CTL SKIP_APL2   ⍝ ⎕NC of GNU APL names/classes differs
      ⎕NC '⍵'
6

      ]FILE_CTL NO_SKIP
      ⎕FX 'Z←⍵ B' 'Z←B+1'
1

      ]FILE_CTL SKIP_APL2   ⍝ lambdas are a GNU APL extension; ⎕NC of GNU APL names/classes differs
      ⎕NC '⍵'
6

      ⍵ 5
VALUE ERROR+
      ⍵ 5
      ^

      )MORE
Offending symbol: ⍵ (U+2375)

      ⍝ control: the same bad name is rejected as F2's left operand too
      ⍝
      ]FILE_CTL NO_SKIP
      ⎕FX 'Z←F ⍺' 'Z←⍺+1'
1

      ⍝ regression (Bugs28 #100(b)): ⍞ has its own distinguished Symbol
      ⍝ (Workspace::get_v_Quad_QUOTE()), tokenized separately from (and
      ⍝ not covered by) Avec::is_quad()'s plain ⎕ check, even though ⍞
      ⍝ is exactly as much a distinguished name as ⎕ itself -- so it was
      ⍝ still accepted here even after the #89 fix above.
      ⍝
      ]FILE_CTL SKIP_APL2   ⍝ ⎕NC of GNU APL names/classes differs
      ⎕NC '⍞'
5

      ]FILE_CTL NO_SKIP
      ⎕FX 'Z←F1 ⍞' 'Z←B'
1

      ]FILE_CTL SKIP_APL2   ⍝ ⎕NC of GNU APL names/classes differs
      ⎕NC '⍞'
5

      ⍝ control: ⍺ used as an operator's bracket-axis subject (not F0/
      ⍝ F1/F2/LO/OP/A/B/Z itself) was already correctly rejected before
      ⍝ this fix -- kept here for contrast with the cases just above.
      ⍝
      ]FILE_CTL NO_SKIP
      ⎕FX 'Z←⍺[X]B' 'Z←X'
1

      ⍝ regression (Bugs28 #92): monadic ⎕FX silently replaced a locked
      ⍝ function (UserFunction::fix()'s cant_be_defined() guard tested
      ⍝ only is_called()/name-class, never the lock bit, unlike the ∇
      ⍝ editor's own check), and the replacement was not itself locked;
      ⍝ 10⎕CR and both ⎕TF forms had no lock test at all and disclosed
      ⍝ the full body. Dyadic ⎕FX (with an explicit properties left
      ⍝ argument) is deliberately exempt -- that IS the documented way
      ⍝ to change a locked function's properties, including its lock
      ⍝ bit, and testcases/Quad_FX.tc's own "execution properties"
      ⍝ regression above already relies on it.
      ⍝
      1 0 0 0 ⎕FX 'Z←M B' 'Z←B+2'
M

      ⎕CR 'M'
      10 ⎕CR 'M'
DOMAIN ERROR+
      10 ⎕CR 'M'
      ^  ^

      )MORE
10 ⎕CR: 'M' is locked; its definition cannot be disclosed.

      1 ⎕TF 'M'
DOMAIN ERROR+
      1 ⎕TF 'M'
      ^ ^

      )MORE
⎕TF: 'M' is locked; its definition cannot be disclosed.

      2 ⎕TF 'M'
DOMAIN ERROR+
      2 ⎕TF 'M'
      ^ ^

      )MORE
⎕TF: 'M' is locked; its definition cannot be disclosed.

      ⎕FX 'Z←M B' 'Z←99'
DEFN ERROR+
      ⎕FX 'Z←M B' 'Z←99'
      ^

      )MORE
Attempt to re-define locked function 'M'. ⎕EX it first.

      )SIC

      ⍝ control: dyadic ⎕FX with an explicit properties vector may
      ⍝ still redefine (and, here, unlock) M
      ⍝
      0 0 0 0 ⎕FX 'Z←M B' 'Z←88'
M

      ⎕CR 'M'
Z←M B
Z←88 

      )ERASE M

      ⍝ regression (Bugs28 #100(i), Bugs35 #55): a '...' (or "..." or «...»)
      ⍝ string that never closes on its own function-body line is rejected,
      ⍝ regardless of the OLD-MULTI-LINE-STRINGS preference (which only
      ⍝ allows "..." strings spanning several lines, joined before
      ⍝ tokenization). See also verify_old_multi_line_strings.sh.
      ⍝
      )ERASE ZZ100I
      ⎕FX 'ZZ100I' 'A←''abc' 'B←5'
2

      ⎕FX 'ZZ100I' 'A←«abc' 'B←5'
2

      ⎕NC 'ZZ100I'
0

      ⎕FX 'Z←ZZ100I' 'Z←"abc' 'def"'
ZZ100I

      ZZ100I
 abc def 

      )ERASE ZZ100I

      ⍝ ==================================


